</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUKIMOTO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO SHINYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUNATO, NAOMICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKUNO, TOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUKIMOTO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, SHINYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p> A pneumatic tire, particularly a pneumatic radial tire for heavy duty in which uneven wear resistance and noise resistance are improved without impairing a wet performance and a steering stability on a dry road surface and which provides a block type tread pattern comprising at least three main grooves extending in circumferential direction in the center area of a tread, S-shaped or Z-shaped block rows disposed between the main grooves, adjacent blocks in a row overlapping partly with each other in the circumferential direction, and shoulder block rows disposed in both side areas of the tread.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un pneumatique, en particulier un pneumatique radial solide présentant une résistance à l'usure irrégulière et une résistance au bruit améliorées, sans altération du comportement à l'état humide et de la stabilité de direction sur un revêtement de route sec. Le pneumatique selon l'invention présente des dessins de la bande de roulement de type en bloc comprenant au moins trois creux principaux s'étendant dans une direction circonférentielle dans la zone centrale d'une bande de roulement; des rangées de blocs en forme de S ou en forme de Z disposées entre les creux principaux; des blocs contigus dans une rangée se superposant en partie dans la direction circonférentielle; et des rangées d'épaulement en bloc disposées dans les deux zones latérales de la bande de roulement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>